      "html" : "<\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-176789\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-176789\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div>The installation of wood shingles shall comply with the provisions of this section and <Link class=\"Jump\" to=\"{{ pathname: '\/codes\/newyorkcity\/latest\/NYCadmin\/0-0-0-176788', hash: '#JD_BCTable1507.8' }}\">Table 1507.8<\/Link>.<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-176790\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-176790\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><a name=\"JD_BCTable1507.8\" id=\"JD_BCTable1507.8\" title=\"BC Table 1507.8\"><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: bold;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Table 1507.8<br><\/br>Wood Shingle and Shake Installation<\/span><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-176791\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-176791\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div>",
      "id" : "17139-html-1",
      "kind" : "html",
      "plainText" : "The installation of wood shingles shall comply with the provisions of this section and Table 1507.8 .\n\n Table 1507.8\n Wood Shingle and Shake Installation"
    },
    {
      "html" : "<ScrollTable><div class=\"xsl-table xsl-table--header\"><table cellSpacing=\"0\" style=\"width: 720px&#10;                ;\"><colgroup><col width=\"33.333%&#10;              \"><\/col><col width=\"33.333%&#10;              \"><\/col><col width=\"33.333%&#10;              \"><\/col><\/colgroup><tbody><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:.075in;padding-right:.075in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><span style=\"font-weight: bold;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Roof Item<\/span>&#160;<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:.075in;padding-right:.075in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><span style=\"font-weight: bold;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Wood Shingles <\/span><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:.075in;padding-right:.075in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><span style=\"font-weight: bold;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Wood Shakes<\/span>&#160;<\/div><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><div class=\"xsl-table xsl-table--body\"><table cellSpacing=\"0\" style=\"width: 720px&#10;                ;\"><colgroup><col width=\"33.333%&#10;              \"><\/col><col width=\"33.333%&#10;              \"><\/col><col width=\"33.333%&#10;              \"><\/col><\/colgroup><tbody><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:.075in;padding-right:.075in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><span style=\"font-weight: bold;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Roof Item<\/span>&#160;<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:.075in;padding-right:.075in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><span style=\"font-weight: bold;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Wood Shingles <\/span><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:.075in;padding-right:.075in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><span style=\"font-weight: bold;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Wood Shakes<\/span>&#160;<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t1.&#160;&#160;&#160;Roof slope<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Wood shingles shall be installed on slopes of not less than three units vertical in 12 units horizontal (3:12).<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Wood shakes shall be installed on slopes of not less than four units vertical in 12 units horizontal (4:12).<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t2.&#160;&#160;&#160;Deck requirement<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;Temperate climate<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Shingles shall be applied to roofs with solid or spaced sheathing. Where spaced sheathing is used, sheathing boards shall be not less than 1\" &#215; 4\" nominal dimensions and shall be spaced on centers equal to the weather exposure to coincide with the placement of fasteners.<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Shakes shall be applied to roofs with solid or spaced sheathing. Where spaced sheathing is used, sheathing boards shall be not less than 1\" &#215; 4\" nominal dimensions and shall be spaced on centers equal to the weather exposure to coincide with the placement of fasteners. When1\" &#215; 4\" spaced sheathing is installed at 10 inches, boards must be installed between the sheathing boards.<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;Ice forming along the eaves causing a backup of water.<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Solid sheathing required.<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Solid sheathing is required.<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t3.&#160;&#160;&#160;Interlayment<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>No requirements.<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Interlayment shall comply with ASTM D 226, Type 1.<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t4.&#160;&#160;&#160;Underlayment<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;Temperate climate<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Underlayment shall comply with ASTM D 226, Type 1.<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Underlayment shall comply with ASTM D 226, Type 1.<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;Ice forming along the eaves causing a backup of water.<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>An ice barrier that consists of at least two layers of underlayment cemented together or of a self-adhering polymer-modified bitumen sheet shall extend from the eave's edge to a point at least 24 inches inside the exterior wall line of the building.<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>An ice barrier that consists of at least two layers of underlayment cemented together or of a self-adhering polymer-modified bitumen sheet shall extend from the lowest eave's edge of all roof surfaces to a point at least 24 inches inside the exterior wall line of the building.<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t5.&#160;&#160;&#160;Application<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;Attachment<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Fasteners for wood shingles shall be hot-dipped galvanized or Type 304 (Type 316 for coastal areas) stainless steel with a minimum penetration of 0.75 inch into the sheathing. For sheathing less than 0.5 inch thick, the fasteners shall extend through the sheathing.<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Fasteners for wood shakes shall be hot-dipped galvanized or Type 304 (Type 316 for coastal areas) with a minimum penetration of 0.75 inch into the sheathing. For sheathing less than 0.5 inch thick, the fasteners shall extend through the sheathing.<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;No. of fasteners<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Two per shingle.<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Two per shake.<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;Exposure<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Weather exposures shall not exceed those set forth in <Link class=\"Jump\" to=\"{{ pathname: '\/codes\/newyorkcity\/latest\/NYCadmin\/0-0-0-176811', hash: '#JD_BCTable1507.8.7' }}\">Table 1507.8.7<\/Link><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Weather exposures shall not exceed those set forth in <Link class=\"Jump\" to=\"{{ pathname: '\/codes\/newyorkcity\/latest\/NYCadmin\/0-0-0-176841', hash: '#JD_BCTable1507.9.8' }}\">Table 1507.9.8<\/Link><\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;Method<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Shingles shall be laid with a side lap of not less than 1.5 inches between joints in courses, and no two joints in any three adjacent courses shall be in direct alignment. Spacing between shingles shall be 0.25 to 0.375 inch.<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>Shakes shall be laid with a side lap of not less than 1.5 inches between joints in adjacent courses. Spacing between shakes shall not be less than 0.375 inch or more than 0.625 inch for shakes and taper sawn shakes of naturally durable wood and shall be 0.25 to 0.375 inch for preservative-treated taper sawn shakes.<\/div><\/td><\/tr><tr><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;Flashing<\/div><\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>In accordance with Section 1507.8.8.<\/div><\/td><td style=\"word-wrap:break-word;padding-left:0.022in;padding-right:0.022in;padding-top:.022in;padding-bottom:.022in;border-top:1pt solid #000000;border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-left:1pt solid #000000;border-right:1pt solid #000000;\"><div>In accordance with Section 1507.9.9.<\/div><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><tfoot><tr><td><\/td><td><\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/tfoot><\/table><\/div><\/ScrollTable>",
      "id" : "17139-table-2",
      "kind" : "table"
    },
    {
      "html" : "<\/div><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-176792\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-176792\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\">For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm, &#176;C = ((&#176;F) - 32)\/1.8.<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><\/div>",
      "id" : "17139-html-3",
